Anubis on Debian (Keel Linux build)
===================================

Instances
---------

anubis@.service is a template: anubis@NAME reads its flags from
/etc/anubis/NAME.env and its signing key from /etc/anubis/NAME.key.
Nothing is enabled or started by the package. /etc/anubis/default.env is
an example instance that listens on 127.0.0.1:8923 (metrics on
127.0.0.1:9090) and forwards to 127.0.0.1:3000.

Anubis belongs behind the web server, never at the edge: keep BIND on the
loopback (or a unix socket) and let nginx terminate TLS and pass X-Real-IP.

The signing key
---------------

The key signs the cookie a browser receives after solving the challenge.
It is the hex-encoded 32-byte ed25519 seed, in a file owned by root with
mode 0600:

  install -m 0600 /dev/null /etc/anubis/default.key
  openssl rand -hex 32 > /etc/anubis/default.key

Before each start the unit copies the file, as root, to
/run/anubis/NAME/signing-key, owned by the instance's dynamic user with
mode 0400, and points ED25519_PRIVATE_KEY_HEX_FILE at it; the copy goes
with the runtime directory when the instance stops. The key is never in
the environment file. Without the file the instance does not start: an instance
with a random key would make every visitor solve the challenge again after
each restart, and on a set of nodes after each failover. Every node behind
the same address must hold the same key.

Policy
------

/etc/anubis/botPolicies.yaml is upstream's default policy. Search engine
crawlers (Googlebot, Bingbot, Applebot, DuckDuckBot and others) are
allowed only from their published address ranges, or by forward-confirmed
reverse DNS for Yandex; the same user agent from any other address is
weighed like any browser and challenged. The rules marked "Requires a
subscription to Thoth" (country and ASN) do nothing without THOTH_URL and
THOTH_TOKEN.

nginx
-----

  location / {
      proxy_set_header Host $host;
      proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
      proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
      proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8923;
  }

See /usr/share/doc/anubis/nginx.mdx.
